{"id": "EUVD-2026-86053", "enisaUuid": "17dbb36c-a747-3dc1-9086-6d42e521b496", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: qrtr: fix node refcount leak on ctrl packet alloc failure\n\nqrtr_send_resume_tx() calls qrtr_node_lookup() which takes a\nreference on the returned node. If the subsequent call to\nqrtr_alloc_ctrl_packet() fails due to memory allocation failure, the\nfunction returns -ENOMEM without calling qrtr_node_release() to\nrelease the node reference.\n\nAdd qrtr_node_release(node) before returning on the allocation failure\npath to properly release the reference.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:03:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:25", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/78d066ecac9ce50441d4affae0df2093c4c3e62e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f3e90fbcd2d5ec1632bc2e8cdd1218f56bcb5fcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c3515740174b778d0ee44acc477b51a6478da6b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f76a39c45182d9137e053081cee9f2c197404ce6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/477353db343663d5502ca442c6de785d2f23f273", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d969c98732a4d42212ec580dd5bbad53f246103", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b09ff54114566864eea59020f6b69c5bb325b9d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x3xx-p253-pwh4", "CVE-2026-97440"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0673bf4e-705b-3f19-918c-edcac3d2950b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb6530b99fafea6c0636c4640bd21301d12cdbc9 <477353db343663d5502ca442c6de785d2f23f273"}, {"id": "4c2d5fab-fedd-319d-be21-f31b3fe02175", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cb6530b99fafea6c0636c4640bd21301d12cdbc9 <c3515740174b778d0ee44acc477b51a6478da6b8"}, {"id": "5005eb26-b466-37fb-b76e-a7b7c12bdd1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.6"}, {"id": "55962b84-9d52-364a-a6f4-ad4192bf421d", "product": 